{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"texture influence in blender python texture influence in blender python","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","fileName":"Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Texture Influence in Blender Python","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"texture influence in blender python texture influence in blender python","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","fileName":"Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Texture Influence in Blender Python","heading":"Texture Influence in Blender Python","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"In the Blender version described by the source, a texture can influence diffuse appearance, shading interactions, specular response, or rendered geometric detail. A color image can define surface color, while a normal-style influence can make a flat mesh render as if it contains ridges without altering its vertices.\n\nInfluence describes what a texture changes, not where its values come from. The same image or procedural texture type can be configured for different effects, and several influences can contribute to one material. Programmatic texturing must therefore specify both the texture data and its role in the final shading result.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"texture influence in blender python texture influence in blender python","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","fileName":"Texture Influence in Blender Python.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Texture Influence in Blender Python","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}